<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="fb463aaa"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="54523a40">&lt;p&gt;
    Defining an architecture governance model for an organization should be driven by the objectives that have been
    identified for the governance functions. The objectives will drive the definition of measures, processes and roles and
    responsibilities. Here are some standard set of objectives:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To effectively resolve design decision impact
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To align architecture alignment and quality
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To manage architecture change control and alignment with defined target architecture vision
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
